Let $\alpha=\arctan\frac{5}{12}$, so $\tan\alpha=\frac{5}{12}$.
Since $-\frac{\pi}{2}<\alpha<\frac{\pi}{2}$ and $\tan\alpha>0$, $\alpha$ is in quadrant 1.
The reference triangle has opposite side $5$ and adjacent side $12$.
$\begin{aligned}h&=\sqrt{5^2+12^2}\\&=13\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(3.6,0)--(0,1.5)--cycle;
\draw (0.18,0)--(0.18,0.18)--(0,0.18);
\draw (3.05,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=157.38,radius=0.55];
\path (1.8,0) node[below] {$12$} (0,0.75) node[left] {$5$} (1.8,0.75) node[above right] {$13$} (2.65,0.2) node {$\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\sin\left(\arctan\frac{5}{12}\right)\\&=\frac{5}{13}\end{aligned}$

Let $\alpha=\arcsin\left(-\frac{2}{7}\right)$, so $\sin\alpha=-\frac{2}{7}$.
Since $-\frac{\pi}{2}\le\alpha\le\frac{\pi}{2}$ and $\sin\alpha<0$, $\alpha$ is in quadrant 4. Its reference angle is $-\alpha$.
Use positive side lengths $2$ and $7$ in the reference triangle.
$\begin{aligned}a&=\sqrt{7^2-2^2}\\&=\sqrt{45}\\&=3\sqrt{5}\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(3.354,0)--(0,1)--cycle;
\draw (0.16,0)--(0.16,0.16)--(0,0.16);
\draw (2.754,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=163.40,radius=0.6];
\path (1.677,0) node[below] {$3\sqrt{5}$} (0,0.5) node[left] {$2$} (1.677,0.5) node[above right] {$7$} (2.35,0.2) node {$-\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The tangent is negative in quadrant 4.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\tan\left(\arcsin\left(-\frac{2}{7}\right)\right)\\&=-\frac{2}{3\sqrt{5}}\\&=-\frac{2\sqrt{5}}{15}\end{aligned}$

Let $\alpha=\arccos\left(-\frac{7}{25}\right)$, so $\cos\alpha=-\frac{7}{25}$.
Since $0\le\alpha\le\pi$ and $\cos\alpha<0$, $\alpha$ is in quadrant 2. Its reference angle is $\pi-\alpha$.
The reference triangle has adjacent side $7$ and hypotenuse $25$.
$\begin{aligned}o&=\sqrt{25^2-7^2}\\&=24\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.05,0)--(0,3.6)--cycle;
\draw (0.16,0)--(0.16,0.16)--(0,0.16);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=106.26,radius=0.4];
\path (0.525,0) node[below] {$7$} (0,1.8) node[left] {$24$} (0.525,1.8) node[above right] {$25$} (1.05,0.65) node[right] {$\pi-\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) The sine is positive in quadrant 2.
$\sin\alpha=\frac{24}{25}$.
(b) The tangent is negative in quadrant 2.
$\tan\alpha=-\frac{24}{7}$.

Let $\alpha=\arctan\left(-\frac{4}{7}\right)$, so $\tan\alpha=-\frac{4}{7}$.
Since $-\frac{\pi}{2}<\alpha<\frac{\pi}{2}$ and $\tan\alpha<0$, $\alpha$ is in quadrant 4. Its reference angle is $-\alpha$.
The reference triangle has opposite side $4$ and adjacent side $7$.
$\begin{aligned}h&=\sqrt{4^2+7^2}\\&=\sqrt{65}\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2.8,0)--(0,1.6)--cycle;
\draw (0.18,0)--(0.18,0.18)--(0,0.18);
\draw (2.25,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=150.26,radius=0.55];
\path (1.4,0) node[below] {$7$} (0,0.8) node[left] {$4$} (1.4,0.8) node[above right] {$\sqrt{65}$} (1.85,0.25) node {$-\alpha$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The cosine is positive in quadrant 4.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\cos\left(\arctan\left(-\frac{4}{7}\right)\right)\\&=\frac{7}{\sqrt{65}}\\&=\frac{7\sqrt{65}}{65}\end{aligned}$

